{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>El, to a living creature</b> — The [final] alef has a kamatz gadol, because it is in construct state and the noun governed by it is implied, like שפעת אני רואה. The meaning: a wild animal of the field." "<b>And Your turtledove</b> — Like שתי תורים (two turtledoves). And some say: לחית is like גער חית קנה, חית פלשתים."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 74, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:32.114421328Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}